  "TITLE": "Phase Transitions<br>and the Critical Point",
  "LEAD": "Heat water and at 100&deg;C it doesn&rsquo;t just get hotter &mdash; it abruptly becomes steam, a jump in density. But raise the pressure and that jump shrinks, until at the critical point it vanishes: liquid and gas become indistinguishable, and fluctuations ripple at every scale. A system balanced there is why a trivial nudge can sway a crowd or a market perched at its own tipping point.",
